    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present to the market this traditional four-bedroom farmhouse situated in the townland of Drumaveg, Moycullen on a plot of just under 2 acres. Offering a good range of accommodation over two floors, the property is complemented by a number of outbuildings and land which presents an opportunity for those seeking an established countryside home within easy reach of Moycullen Village.The property approached through a tree lined driveway enjoys a lovely woodland garden to the front in addition to two fine grazing paddocks with site potential in the front field. The accommodation has a practical and comfortable layout. The entrance hall leads to the main living room, a welcoming space with a solid-fuel stove forming the focal point of the room. The kitchen and dining area provides ample space for everyday family use, with the kitchen fitted with a range of wall and base units and plumbed for both a dishwasher and washing machine.A particularly beneficial feature of the property is the spacious double bedroom located on the ground floor, complete with its own en-suite wet room comprising a wet-room style shower, WC and WHB. This provides the convenience and flexibility of having both bedroom and bathroom accommodation at entrance level.On the first floor, there are three further bedrooms together with the main family bathroom. One of the bedrooms benefits from dual-aspect windows, allowing for excellent natural light, while the remaining bedrooms are well proportioned and offer useful storage. The main bathroom is fitted with a bath and separate shower, together with a WC and WHB.The farmhouse offers scope for upgrading and modernisation, allowing a new owner to enhance the existing accommodation over time and put their own stamp on the home.Outside, a number of outbuildings and a hay shed provide useful additional storage and are a valuable feature of the property, adding to its traditional farmhouse character and overall versatility. Drumaveg offers a peaceful countryside setting while remaining convenient to Moycullen Village and its range of shops, schools, cafés, sporting facilities and everyday amenities. Galway City is also readily accessible, making the property well positioned for those wishing to enjoy a rural setting while retaining convenient access to both Moycullen and the city.With four bedrooms, including a ground-floor en-suite bedroom, useful outbuildings and excellent scope for further improvement, this traditional farmhouse offers an appealing opportunity for those looking for a countryside home in the Moycullen area."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nWelcoming entrance hall providing access to the principal ground-floor accommodation, with staircase leading to the first floor.\n\nLiving Room - \nGenerous living room featuring a freestanding solid-fuel stove set on a tiled hearth, with windows providing good natural light.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nSpacious kitchen and dining area offering excellent everyday living space. The kitchen is fitted with a range of wall and base units with worktop space and sink, and is plumbed for both a washing machine and dishwasher.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nSpacious ground-floor double bedroom with windows providing natural light and the benefit of an adjoining en-suite wet room.\n\nEn-Suite Wet Room - \nFully tiled and comprising a wet-room style shower, WC and WHB.\n\nLanding - \nBright first-floor landing with timber flooring and built-in storage, providing access to three bedrooms and the main bathroom.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nGenerous double bedroom with dual-aspect windows providing excellent natural light and ample space for bedroom furniture.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nWell-proportioned bedroom with fitted wardrobe storage and a window providing natural light.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nBright and well-proportioned bedroom with built-in storage.\n\nMain Bathroom - \nSpacious bathroom comprising a separate shower enclosure, bath, WC and WHB, with tiled finishes and window providing natural light.\n\nRound-Top Shed - \nSubstantial round-top shed with lean-to structures to either side, providing excellent covered storage and general-purpose space.\n\nStorage Shed - \nUseful separate storage shed offering additional secure storage space.\n\nGeneral-Purpose Shed - \nVersatile detached shed offering excellent potential for a variety of uses, including a workshop, home office, gym, hobby room or additional storage, subject to any necessary works or permissions.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Traditional four-bedroom farmhouse in Drumaveg, Moycullen on just under 2 acres of land</li><li> Four well-proportioned bedrooms arranged over two floors</li><li> Ground-floor double bedroom with en-suite wet room</li><li> Comfortable living room with solid-fuel stove</li><li> Spacious kitchen and dining area</li><li> Main bathroom with separate bath and shower</li><li> Number of useful outbuildings and hay shed</li><li> Excellent scope for upgrading and modernisation</li><li> Peaceful rural setting within easy reach of Moycullen Village</li><li> OFCH</ul>"
      },
